.TH OPENLIVEGAMER4K-CONTROL 1 "September 2026" "openlivegamer4k 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openlivegamer4k-control \- inspect and preview the AVerMedia Live Gamer 4K capture card
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBopenlivegamer4k-control\fP [\fB\-\-backend\fP=\fIbackend\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBopenlivegamer4k-control\fP is a native GTK 4 (X11/Wayland) control
application for the OpenLiveGamer4K (GC573) V4L2 capture driver.
.PP
By default it runs in \fBread-only status mode\fP: it enumerates and
queries the device (driver name, input, configured format, size and
rate) without allocating streaming buffers or changing capture
settings, so it is safe to run while OBS or another V4L2 client owns
the node.
.PP
Selecting \fIStart preview\fP switches the application to the exclusive
V4L2 node, negotiates the selected format, size and rate, and streams
frames to the window. \fIStop preview\fP releases the device
immediately. If the node is already in use, the application reports the
failure; it never stops or preempts another client.
.PP
The application runs unprivileged, opens no network connections, and
collects no telemetry. It launches even when no GC573 node is present
and reports that the device is absent.
.SH HDMI AUDIO
Audio is enabled by default on driver load; an explicit disable option is respected. Enabling or disabling
uses a narrow polkit helper to reload an idle driver and reconnect HDMI.
Other clients must close the device first. The GUI remains unprivileged.
The five-second HDMI test supports stereo 48 kHz LPCM only and retains no
recording. Concurrent V4L2 video and ALSA audio capture are supported.
Video stop or HDMI recovery can interrupt audio; restart capture if needed.
Long-duration A/V synchronization remains unqualified. No boot setting
is changed and no report is uploaded automatically.
.SH REPORTING PROBLEMS
Save a diagnostic report while the problem is present, review the JSON, then
use the Report a problem on GitHub link to open the guided issue form.
Include the input mode, capture settings and reproduction steps. No report is
uploaded automatically; the collector does not record media or stop capture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fP=\fIbackend\fP, \fB\-b\fP \fIbackend\fP
Device backend to use. \fIauto\fP (default) probes
\fI/dev/video0\fP..\fI/dev/video31\fP for a card whose V4L2 name is
"Live Gamer 4K". \fImock\fP opens a deterministic in-process device
that reports the full GC573 capability set; useful for offline
development and testing without hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/dev/videoN\fP
V4L2 capture node created by the \fBgc573_pure\fP kernel module.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBv4l2\-ctl\fP(1), the \fIopenlivegamer4k-dkms\fP package README
(\fI/usr/share/doc/openlivegamer4k-dkms/README.Debian.gz\fP).
